      "writtenOn": "2024-10-14T09:01:32Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Correct me if I\u0027m wrong:\n\nThe `IBinder` implements `equals` so the same object can be re-identified across `requestDownstream()` and `releaseDownstream()` calls. On the contrary, `IIpv4AddressRequester` doesn\u0027t implement `equals` so it cannot be re-identified (I previously verified this locally).\n\nAn alternative is to create a class wrapping the `IIpv4AddressRequester` object and we implement `equals` based on the `IBinder.equals`. Updated the code to use this alternative.",
      "parentUuid": "85e71811_f4e9755b",
